think baton extension — recommend no new extension; a baton is a .kyri document with format baton-v1, exactly as a session log is format session-log-v1; one notation, many formats, never a proliferation of extensions
think unify tilaks — yes in principle; a tilak is our word for the elder's mark, a type-marked record; one shared til/ home the whole stack draws from is right, yet a real architectural sitting worth its own round, not a snap decision; Scribe uses tilaks, never reinvents them
think the folder grid — recommend map, don't restructure; the reframe released the obligation to mirror the elder's gen/sur/app/sys, and the warm module-named dirs are clearer; we already have these under warmer names (rishi=gen, tilaks/til=sur/mar, pond=app, glow/rishi/rye core=sys, stdlib=lib, witnesses=tes) — seat the mapping, the vane-parallel the tree already favors
think auditing sweep — today's witnesses prove the happy zone; an adversarial/edge auditing sweep across every module is a worthy next-season initiative, recorded; lexicon horizon integration is already the standing practice (horizon → landed on witness)
obs seated the counsel as a design note (recommendations for his word), restructured nothing, built no folders — the reframe is honored best by naming what we already are
